{
  "kanda": "kishkindha",
  "sarga": 36,
  "title": "Sugreeva's apology pacifies Lakshmana",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga36/kishkindhasans36.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga36/kishkindhaitrans36.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Sugreeva's apology pacifies Lakshmana. On knowing that Lakshmana is pacified by Tara's reasoning Sugreeva makes his apologetic statement and affirms his support to Rama. Then Lakshmana's rage comes to a halt and he too is appeased by the open declaration of Sugreeva about his adherence to Rama, and Lakshmana asks him to come to Rama."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये किष्किन्ध काण्डे षट् त्रिंशः सर्गः"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "4.36.1",
      "label": "4.36.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "इति उक्तः तारया वाक्यम् प्रश्रितम् धर्म संहितम् |\nमृदु स्वभावः सौमित्रिः प्रतिजग्राह तत् वचः",
      "iast": "iti uktaḥ tārayā vākyam praśritam dharma saṃhitam |\nmṛdu svabhāvaḥ saumitriḥ pratijagrāha tat vacaḥ",
      "translation": "In that way when Tara has submissively argued with words containing probity, Saumitri gave assent to her perspective as he is soft by his nature.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "iti taarayaa",
          "iast": "iti tārayā",
          "devanagari": "इति तारया",
          "meaning": "in that way, by Tara",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "prashritam",
          "iast": "praśritam",
          "devanagari": "प्रश्रितं",
          "meaning": "having submissiveness -words",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dharma samhitam vaakyam",
          "iast": "dharma samhitam vākyam",
          "devanagari": "धर्म सम्हितं वाक्यं",
          "meaning": "probity, imbibed, sentence - argument",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "uktaH",
          "iast": "uktaḥ",
          "devanagari": "उक्तः",
          "meaning": "he who is said - Lakshmana",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mR^idu svabhaavaH saumitriH",
          "iast": "mṛdu svabhāvaḥ saumitriḥ",
          "devanagari": "मृदु स्वभावः सौमित्रिः",
          "meaning": "of tender, nature - soft-natured one, Soumitri",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "tat vacaH prati jagraaha",
          "iast": "tat vacaḥ prati jagrāha",
          "devanagari": "तत् वचः प्रति जग्राह",
          "meaning": "that, word, received - assented her perspective.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.36.2",
      "label": "4.36.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "तस्मिन् प्रतिगृहीते तु वाक्ये हरि गण ईश्वरः |\nलक्ष्मणात् सुमहत् त्रासम् वस्त्रम् क्लिन्नम् इव अत्यजत्",
      "iast": "tasmin pratigṛhīte tu vākye hari gaṇa īśvaraḥ |\nlakṣmaṇāt sumahat trāsam vastram klinnam iva atyajat",
      "translation": "And when Lakshmana conceded to that argument of Tara, Sugreeva, the king of monkey-troops, got rid of his highly intense scare of Lakshmana, like the riddance of a dampened cloth.",
      "notes": [
        "This may be said as: 'Sugreeva lost his scare as a dampened cloth looses its water on squeezing it. But here there is no squeezing."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "tasmin pratigR^ihiite tu vaakye",
          "iast": "tasmin pratigṛhīte tu vākye",
          "devanagari": "तस्मिन् प्रतिगृहीते तु वाक्ये",
          "meaning": "that [word,] on conceding, but, [by Lakshmana]",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "hari gaNa iishvaraH",
          "iast": "hari gaṇa īśvaraḥ",
          "devanagari": "हरि गण ईश्वरः",
          "meaning": "monkey, troops, king",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "lakSmaNaat su mahat traasam",
          "iast": "lakṣmaṇāt su mahat trāsam",
          "devanagari": "लक्ष्मणात् सु महत् त्रासं",
          "meaning": "of Lakshmana, highly, intense, scare",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "klinnam vastram iva",
          "iast": "klinnam vastram iva",
          "devanagari": "क्लिन्नं वस्त्रं इव",
          "meaning": "cloth, dampened, as with",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 10
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.36.3",
      "label": "4.36.3",
      "numbers": [
        3
      ],
      "devanagari": "ततः कण्ठ गतम् माल्यम् चित्रम् बहु गुणम् महत् |\nचिच्छेद विमदः च आसीत् सुग्रीवो वानर ईश्वरः",
      "iast": "tataḥ kaṇṭha gatam mālyam citram bahu guṇam mahat |\nciccheda vimadaḥ ca āsīt sugrīvo vānara īśvaraḥ",
      "translation": "Sugreeva, the king of vanara-s, then ripped apart the superb garland which is so far enwreathing his neck, and which has several strands according several gratifications, and he also became sober as though the insobriety is ripped from his mind.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "tataH",
          "iast": "tataḥ",
          "devanagari": "ततः",
          "meaning": "then",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vaanara iishvaraH sugriivaH",
          "iast": "vānara īśvaraḥ sugrīvaḥ",
          "devanagari": "वानर ईश्वरः सुग्रीवः",
          "meaning": "Vanara-s, king, Sugreeva",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 12
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kaNTha gatam",
          "iast": "kaṇṭha gatam",
          "devanagari": "कण्ठ गतं",
          "meaning": "neck, enwreathing",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "itrans": "citram",
          "iast": "citram",
          "devanagari": "चित्रं",
          "meaning": "admirable",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bahu guNam",
          "iast": "bahu guṇam",
          "devanagari": "बहु गुणं",
          "meaning": "having several, attributes [according gratifications, or, one with several strands]",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mahat maalyam",
          "iast": "mahat mālyam",
          "devanagari": "महत् माल्यं",
          "meaning": "superb, garland",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "cicCheda",
          "iast": "ciccheda",
          "devanagari": "चिच्छेद",
          "meaning": "ripped apart",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vi madaH ca aasiit",
          "iast": "vi madaḥ ca āsīt",
          "devanagari": "वि मदः च आसीत्",
          "meaning": "without, insobriety, also, he became - he became sober.",
          "anvayaIndex": 7,
          "verseIndex": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.36.4",
      "label": "4.36.4",
      "numbers": [
        4
      ],
      "devanagari": "स लक्ष्मणम् भीम बलम् सर्व वानर सत्तमः |\nअब्रवीत् प्रश्रितम् वाक्यम् सुग्रीवः संप्रहर्षयन्",
      "iast": "sa lakṣmaṇam bhīma balam sarva vānara sattamaḥ |\nabravīt praśritam vākyam sugrīvaḥ sampraharṣayan",
      "translation": "Sugreeva who is the most powerful one among all vanara-s, then placatingly spoke this humble sentence to Lakshmana, whose prowess is most formidable.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "sarva vaanara sattamaH",
          "iast": "sarva vānara sattamaḥ",
          "devanagari": "सर्व वानर सत्तमः",
          "meaning": "among all, Vaanara-s, [most] powerful one",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "saH sugriivaH",
          "iast": "saḥ sugrīvaḥ",
          "devanagari": "सः सुग्रीवः",
          "meaning": "he, Sugreeva",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bhiima balam lakSmaNam",
          "iast": "bhīma balam lakṣmaṇam",
          "devanagari": "भीम बलं लक्ष्मणं",
          "meaning": "one with [most] formidable, prowess, to Lakshmana",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sam pra harSayan",
          "iast": "sam pra harṣayan",
          "devanagari": "सं प्र हर्षयन्",
          "meaning": "very, well, to please - placatingly",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "prashritam vaakyam abraviit",
          "iast": "praśritam vākyam abravīt",
          "devanagari": "प्रश्रितं वाक्यं अब्रवीत्",
          "meaning": "humble, sentence, he spoke.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.36.5",
      "label": "4.36.5",
      "numbers": [
        5
      ],
      "devanagari": "प्रनष्टा श्रीः च कीर्तिः च कपि राज्यम् च शाश्वतम् |\nराम प्रसादात् सौमित्रे पुनः च आप्तम् इदम् मया",
      "iast": "pranaṣṭā śrīḥ ca kīrtiḥ ca kapi rājyam ca śāśvatam |\nrāma prasādāt saumitre punaḥ ca āptam idam mayā",
      "translation": "\"My prosperity, prominence and this perpetual kingdom of monkeys are once mislaid, but oh, Soumitri, I regained all this just by the beneficence of Rama.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "saumitre",
          "iast": "saumitre",
          "devanagari": "सौमित्रे",
          "meaning": "O, Soumitri",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "pra naSTaa",
          "iast": "pra naṣṭā",
          "devanagari": "प्र नष्टा",
          "meaning": "completely lost - mislaid",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shriiH ca kiirtiH ca",
          "iast": "śrīḥ ca kīrtiḥ ca",
          "devanagari": "श्रीः च कीर्तिः च",
          "meaning": "prosperity, also, prominence, also",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shaashvatam kapi raajyam ca",
          "iast": "śāśvatam kapi rājyam ca",
          "devanagari": "शाश्वतं कपि राज्यं च",
          "meaning": "perpetual, kingdom, of monkeys, also",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "idam",
          "iast": "idam",
          "devanagari": "इदं",
          "meaning": "all this",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 15
        },
        {
          "itrans": "raama prasaadaat",
          "iast": "rāma prasādāt",
          "devanagari": "राम प्रसादात्",
          "meaning": "at Rama's, beneficence",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mayaa punaH aaptam ca",
          "iast": "mayā punaḥ āptam ca",
          "devanagari": "मया पुनः आप्तं च",
          "meaning": "by me, again, recouped, also.",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.36.6",
      "label": "4.36.6",
      "numbers": [
        6
      ],
      "devanagari": "कः शक्तः तस्य देवस्य ख्यातस्य स्वेन कर्मणा |\nतादृशम् प्रतिकुर्वीत अंशेन अपि नृपात्मज",
      "iast": "kaḥ śaktaḥ tasya devasya khyātasya svena karmaṇā |\ntādṛśam pratikurvīta aṃśena api nṛpātmaja",
      "translation": "\"Who is capable of requiting Rama, oh, prince Lakshmana, even by a fraction of that kind of inestimable help taken from him, as that lord is renowned by actions particular to himself, like daring and eliminating Vali.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "nR^ipa aatmaja",
          "iast": "nṛpa ātmaja",
          "devanagari": "नृप आत्मज",
          "meaning": "O, king's, son [prince]",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "svena karmaNaa khyaatasya",
          "iast": "svena karmaṇā khyātasya",
          "devanagari": "स्वेन कर्मणा ख्यातस्य",
          "meaning": "by his own, course of action, renowned",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 4
        },
        {
          "itrans": "devasya tasya",
          "iast": "devasya tasya",
          "devanagari": "देवस्य तस्य",
          "meaning": "of lord, of him [Rama]",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shaktaH kaH",
          "iast": "śaktaḥ kaḥ",
          "devanagari": "शक्तः कः",
          "meaning": "a capable one, who is",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "amshena api",
          "iast": "amśena api",
          "devanagari": "अम्शेन अपि",
          "meaning": "by fraction, even",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "taadR^isham",
          "iast": "tādṛśam",
          "devanagari": "तादृशं",
          "meaning": "that kind of [inestimable help, or that kind of Rama]",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "prati kurviita",
          "iast": "prati kurvīta",
          "devanagari": "प्रति कुर्वीत",
          "meaning": "who is, in turn, to do [requital, or, doing against, repudiate.]",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.36.7",
      "label": "4.36.7",
      "numbers": [
        7
      ],
      "devanagari": "सीताम् प्राप्स्यति धर्मात्मा वधिष्यति च रावणम् |\nसहाय मात्रेण मया राघवः स्वेन तेजसा",
      "iast": "sītām prāpsyati dharmātmā vadhiṣyati ca rāvaṇam |\nsahāya mātreṇa mayā rāghavaḥ svena tejasā",
      "translation": "\"Virtue-souled Raghava reacquires Seetha, and even exterminates Ravana by himself with his own resplendence, while I and my assistance remain only in name.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "dharmaatmaa raaghavaH",
          "iast": "dharmātmā rāghavaḥ",
          "devanagari": "धर्मात्मा राघवः",
          "meaning": "virtue-souled, Raghava",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sahaaya maatreNa mayaa",
          "iast": "sahāya mātreṇa mayā",
          "devanagari": "सहाय मात्रेण मया",
          "meaning": "assistance, barely [in name only,] with me - while I and my assistance remain in name",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "svena tejasaa",
          "iast": "svena tejasā",
          "devanagari": "स्वेन तेजसा",
          "meaning": "by his own, resplendence siitaam praapsyati = Seetha, he acquires",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "raavaNam vadhiSyati ca",
          "iast": "rāvaṇam vadhiṣyati ca",
          "devanagari": "रावणं वधिष्यति च",
          "meaning": "Ravana, he exterminates, also.",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.36.8",
      "label": "4.36.8",
      "numbers": [
        8
      ],
      "devanagari": "सहाय कृत्यम् किम् तस्य येन सप्त महाद्रुमाः |\nशैलः च वसुधा चैव बाणेन एकेन दारिताः",
      "iast": "sahāya kṛtyam kim tasya yena sapta mahādrumāḥ |\nśailaḥ ca vasudhā caiva bāṇena ekena dāritāḥ",
      "translation": "\"Basically, why some measures of succour need be extended to him who has ripped seven gigantic-trees, a mountain, and even the earth, all just with one arrow!",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "yena",
          "iast": "yena",
          "devanagari": "येन",
          "meaning": "by whom",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
